  "notes": "To sing or hum softly to oneself, often absent-mindedly or in a relaxed mood. Conveys a warm, gentle image.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Takes を for the song or melody being hummed\n\nALTERNATIVE WRITING:\nCan also be written {口遊|くちずさ}む.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {歌|うた}を{口|くち}ずさむ: to hum a song\n- メロディーを{口|くち}ずさむ: to hum a melody\n- {口|くち}ずさんでいる: to be humming (ongoing)\n- {思|おも}わず{口|くち}ずさむ: to hum without thinking\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {鼻歌|はなうた}を{歌|うた}う: to hum (through the nose)\n- {歌|うた}う: to sing (louder, more deliberate)\n\nREGISTER:\nSlightly literary. Common in written descriptions and narratives.",
